M2 inline reference material
----------------------------

The entity table in Sources/SetzerParser/InlineTables.swift is regenerated
from swift-cmark src/entities.inc at revision
08ddb528923cc1a6527e02b7a1aee9e516ca749a. Scripts/generate_inline_tables.py
records pinned input hashes. The 2,125 entity names are the semicolon-terminated
HTML5 names; CommonMark does not accept the 106 legacy no-semicolon aliases.
The full non-Turkic case-fold table is generated from official Unicode 17.0.0
C/F mappings at https://www.unicode.org/Public/17.0.0/ucd/CaseFolding.txt.
This data is covered by Unicode License V3, permitted by Plan section 8.
Scripts/Data/CaseFolding-17.0.0.txt retains its source header and the input
hash is tested. No runtime Unicode package is required.

M4 GFM extensions
-----------------

GFM tables, task list items, strikethrough, extended autolinks and the tag
filter are ported from cmark-gfm's extensions/table.c, tasklist.c,
strikethrough.c, autolink.c, tagfilter.c and ext_scanners.re, as pinned in
https://github.com/swiftlang/swift-cmark at revision
08ddb528923cc1a6527e02b7a1aee9e516ca749a (a fork of
https://github.com/github/cmark-gfm). The recognition rules are reproduced in
original Swift over GMSetzer's byte/line model; files:
Sources/SetzerParser/GFMBlocks.swift, Sources/SetzerParser/InlineAutolinks.swift,
the strikethrough functions in Sources/SetzerParser/InlineParser.swift and the
tag filter in Sources/SetzerHTML/HTMLRenderer.swift. The same BSD-2-Clause
terms reproduced below apply.

The inline delimiter-stack implementation follows CommonMark's parsing
strategy and the cmark/swift-cmark src/inlines.c openers-bottom algorithm.
The Swift code is an original implementation with value/index storage;
upstream copyright and licence terms are reproduced below. The source-data
copy of the full upstream terms is also in Scripts/Data/cmark-COPYING.

